    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor lineup, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (70.97). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a premium matchup against Hughes, where a favorable park factor and a solid #2 spot in the lineup amplify his base projection. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** is a primary play; his matchup against Meeker (xERA 5.31) provides an ideal environment for him to leverage his lead-off spot. While **Drake Baldwin** faces a slight rain risk, his 67.31 score remains elite due to his lead-off status and the favorable xERA of King. These three players represent our highest projected points of efficiency, balancing park factors with prime lineup positioning to maximize run and RBI potential.\n\nStrategic bench management remains critical given our focus on the scarce SB category. **Nasim Nunez** (55.36) was the most difficult exclusion from the active roster; while his profile fits our tactical needs, he was ultimately benched due to a projected #9 batting order slot, which suppresses his opportunity for counting stats compared to the higher-upside profiles like **Cole Carrigg** or **Jackson Merrill**. We are closely monitoring the 35% rain risk for **Drake Baldwin** and **Jackson Merrill**, which could force mid-game pivots. Additionally, while **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** face a slightly tougher look against Bennett, their combined profile\u2014bolstered by positive BvP trends and the potential for stolen bases against a slower delivery\u2014ensures they remain locked in despite the sub-optimal platoon splits. We will continue to evaluate **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Liam Hicks** as official lineups materialize, as any drop in order could trigger a bench reassessment.",
